WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.023 --> 00:00:08.995
Subtitle created by - <font color="#ffff00">Aorion</font> -
"Warcraft (2016)" ^ (Run time 02:03:06)

2
00:01:23.578 --> 00:01:25.982
There has been a war between
orcs and humans

3
00:01:26.007 --> 00:01:28.605
for as long as
can be remembered.

4
00:01:32.433 --> 00:01:33.959
But there was once a time,

5
00:01:33.984 --> 00:01:37.322
when we did not even know
who our enemy was.

6
00:01:39.423 --> 00:01:43.805
Or what that evil green magic,
the fel, had done to us.

7
00:01:55.542 --> 00:01:58.790
But in the beginning,
how could we have known.

8
00:01:59.176 --> 00:02:01.340
What choice did we have?

9
00:02:02.862 --> 00:02:04.680
Our world was dying.

10
00:02:04.705 --> 00:02:08.327
And I had to find my clan
a new home.

11
00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:18.165
Durotan.

12
00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:21.205
I can feel your eyes.

13
00:02:23.436 --> 00:02:25.786
I thought you were asleep.

14
00:02:26.277 --> 00:02:28.123
I was.

15
00:02:33.057 --> 00:02:38.101
Dreaming of a hunt,
through the snow.

16
00:02:45.524 --> 00:02:47.538
I thought of a name.

17
00:02:48.194 --> 00:02:51.572
Well.
Keep it to yourself, wife.

18
00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:53.791
I'll choose a name
when I meet him.

19
00:02:54.237 --> 00:02:55.956
Or her.

20
00:02:56.415 --> 00:02:57.830
Oh.

21
00:02:58.152 --> 00:03:01.525
And how will the great
Durotan name his son?

22
00:03:02.552 --> 00:03:04.546
If I do not travel with him.

23
00:03:04.571 --> 00:03:06.409
A son?

24
00:03:07.653 --> 00:03:10.033
Can you hide your fat belly?

25
00:03:13.479 --> 00:03:16.072
Better than you can
hide your fat head.

26
00:03:49.888 --> 00:03:52.842
So many clans from one place, Orgrim.

27
00:03:53.045 --> 00:03:56.118
Laughing skull.
Black rock.

28
00:03:56.143 --> 00:03:57.876
All have been summoned.

29
00:03:57.901 --> 00:04:00.530
It will be a mighty warband.

30
00:04:00.924 --> 00:04:03.821
I just wonder
who's left to fight?

31
00:04:03.846 --> 00:04:05.956
Lok'tar ogar!
(Victory or death!)

32
00:04:06.849 --> 00:04:09.300
Victory or death!

33
00:04:11.246 --> 00:04:13.563
Black rock, over there.

34
00:04:13.767 --> 00:04:16.410
How much longer, Blackhand?

35
00:04:16.602 --> 00:04:18.939
We are ready, Gul'dan.

36
00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:21.175
Help me.

37
00:04:21.206 --> 00:04:24.271
My child.
Please let him go.

38
00:04:24.296 --> 00:04:26.065
I beg you.

39
00:04:26.453 --> 00:04:28.760
What did she say?

40
00:04:29.593 --> 00:04:32.316
She begs for you
to free her child.

41
00:04:32.341 --> 00:04:36.610
But I need him.
I need all of them.

42
00:04:55.309 --> 00:04:57.714
Move, half breed.

43
00:05:05.053 --> 00:05:08.860
- What is that?
- Gul'dan's magic.

44
00:05:19.831 --> 00:05:25.265
The fuel of my magic is life.

45
00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:31.066
We only have enough prisoners to
send through our strongest warriors.

46
00:05:31.091 --> 00:05:36.314
But that will be enough.
The enemy is weak.

47
00:05:36.339 --> 00:05:41.977
When we arrive,
we will take them as fuel.

48
00:05:45.351 --> 00:05:49.727
We will build a new portal.
And when it is complete,

49
00:05:49.752 --> 00:05:56.125
we will bring through all...
of the Horde.

50
00:06:50.015 --> 00:06:52.098
Let me go first.

51
00:06:58.753 --> 00:07:00.977
For the Horde!

52
00:07:57.771 --> 00:07:59.619
With child?

53
00:07:59.644 --> 00:08:03.727
You dare bring that burden
into my war band!

54
00:08:05.069 --> 00:08:08.547
Let me go, Blackhand.
Draka!

55
00:08:23.042 --> 00:08:26.611
Push, little one.
Push.

56
00:08:35.122 --> 00:08:36.553
My son.

57
00:09:05.865 --> 00:09:09.514
A new warrior for the Horde.

58
00:09:22.147 --> 00:09:26.273
WARCRAFT

59
00:09:30.132 --> 00:09:33.816
IRONGORGE

60
00:09:35.674 --> 00:09:40.074
Lothar, come.
I have got something for you.

61
00:09:45.845 --> 00:09:49.577
- What is it?
- A mechanical marvel.

62
00:09:49.602 --> 00:09:52.466
It's a boomstick.

63
00:09:57.410 --> 00:09:58.908
Odd.

64
00:10:04.069 --> 00:10:05.858
Take water.

65
00:10:13.405 --> 00:10:16.147
You might want to
head home, big man.

66
00:10:16.925 --> 00:10:19.863
Someone has attacked
one of your garrisons.

67
00:10:19.888 --> 00:10:23.180
It seems your king
needs you, commander.

68
00:10:31.056 --> 00:10:36.354
Stormwind

69
00:10:36.379 --> 00:10:40.201
The entire garrison,
and no one saw anything.

70
00:10:40.226 --> 00:10:41.833
We did find someone.

71
00:10:41.858 --> 00:10:45.439
He was searching the bodies,
here, in the barracks.

72
00:10:48.301 --> 00:10:50.346
In the barracks?

73
00:10:51.323 --> 00:10:54.200
Finally.
Are you in command?

74
00:10:58.369 --> 00:10:59.913
.

75
00:11:03.096 --> 00:11:05.603
That's the mark of the Kirin Tor.

76
00:11:05.912 --> 00:11:08.785
What are you doing in my city,
spell chucker?

77
00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:17.416
Let me complete my examination
of the body across the hall.

78
00:11:18.463 --> 00:11:20.496
Now why would I do that?

79
00:11:20.521 --> 00:11:23.886
Within that body is the
secret to your attacks.

80
00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:45.380
What was that?

81
00:11:46.429 --> 00:11:48.283
You must summon the Guardian.

82
00:11:48.308 --> 00:11:49.869
Medivh?

83
00:11:49.894 --> 00:11:51.998
It should be he
who explains it.

84
00:11:53.743 --> 00:11:56.517
Only the king summons the Guardian.

85
00:11:58.051 --> 00:12:00.085
Get him to Goldshire.

86
00:12:24.171 --> 00:12:27.366
- What kind of beasts?
- Rumors, your Majesty.

87
00:12:27.391 --> 00:12:30.039
How does a garrison of 30 men
disappear without a whisper.

88
00:12:30.064 --> 00:12:31.540
The fel.

89
00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:35.995
Or at least it's influence.

90
00:12:37.523 --> 00:12:39.237
Is this him?

91
00:12:40.383 --> 00:12:42.064
Your Majesty.

92
00:12:43.494 --> 00:12:44.987
Dad.

93
00:12:45.417 --> 00:12:47.209
Thank you, son.

94
00:12:47.853 --> 00:12:50.390
So who are you, mage?

95
00:12:51.053 --> 00:12:54.061
My name is Khadgar.
I'm a Guardian novitiate.

96
00:12:54.234 --> 00:12:55.963
I was.
I renounced my vows.

97
00:12:55.988 --> 00:12:57.760
You mean you're a fugitive?

98
00:12:57.785 --> 00:12:59.761
I'm not hiding.

99
00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:01.782
Your Majesty.

100
00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:06.456
I may have left my training but
I didn't leave my abilities behind.

101
00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:08.238
I senses something.

102
00:13:08.847 --> 00:13:12.936
Dark forces, when it's strong it...
almost has a smell.

103
00:13:12.961 --> 00:13:16.801
Knowing that something so evil was
so close I couldn't just ignore it.

104
00:13:17.642 --> 00:13:18.914
What's going on out there?

105
00:13:18.939 --> 00:13:21.848
Smoke, Sir.
The southeast.

106
00:13:24.097 --> 00:13:26.746
Your Majesty, I urge you to engage
the Guardian with all haste.

107
00:13:26.770 --> 00:13:30.481
- They've reached Elwynn Forest.
- The Grand Hamlet is burning.

108
00:13:33.245 --> 00:13:34.808
An attack?

109
00:13:37.885 --> 00:13:40.711
- What?
- Stop requesting Callan.

110
00:13:40.881 --> 00:13:42.797
Stay out of my business.

111
00:13:42.822 --> 00:13:46.002
He wants to follow in
his father's footsteps.

112
00:13:46.027 --> 00:13:48.102
My son doesn't need your help.

113
00:13:48.127 --> 00:13:50.997
Tread carefully when
you talk to your queen.

114
00:13:54.611 --> 00:13:57.085
You are my sister first.

115
00:13:58.945 --> 00:14:01.160
When was your last visit to Karazhan?

116
00:14:01.185 --> 00:14:04.829
With you.
I don't know... 6 years?

117
00:14:04.854 --> 00:14:07.023
And you had no contact
with Medivh since?

118
00:14:07.048 --> 00:14:08.956
Not for the lack of trying.

119
00:14:08.981 --> 00:14:10.274
Well.

120
00:14:11.159 --> 00:14:13.228
He can't hide from us now.

121
00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:16.952
The Guardian is summoned.

122
00:14:34.426 --> 00:14:35.906
Get on.

123
00:14:42.215 --> 00:14:43.731
Good luck.

124
00:14:47.476 --> 00:14:49.173
Okay.

125
00:15:15.468 --> 00:15:17.326
Let me go!

126
00:15:20.010 --> 00:15:22.650
Frostwolves do not join the hunt?

127
00:15:25.495 --> 00:15:29.114
We prefer our enemies armed
with an axe, not a child.

128
00:15:29.139 --> 00:15:34.844
We have been commanded, Durotan.
Respect the old ways.

129
00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:40.765
There must be a worthy foe
somewhere on this dung heap.

130
00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:42.130
Find them all!

131
00:15:42.155 --> 00:15:45.774
Try not to kill too many,
we need them alive.

132
00:16:18.303 --> 00:16:19.981
Lothar.

133
00:16:20.006 --> 00:16:21.771
Moroes.

134
00:16:21.961 --> 00:16:26.125
Look at you.
You haven't aged a bit.

135
00:16:34.676 --> 00:16:36.256
Where is everyone?

136
00:16:36.281 --> 00:16:37.820
Many things have changed.

137
00:16:37.845 --> 00:16:40.621
The power that must be locked away here,
the knowledge.

138
00:16:40.646 --> 00:16:42.551
Where is he?

139
00:16:43.353 --> 00:16:45.962
I didn't know so many books
even existed.

140
00:16:47.077 --> 00:16:48.681
Wait here.

141
00:16:49.277 --> 00:16:51.808
And try not to touch anything.

142
00:16:52.463 --> 00:16:56.290
- He sees no one?
- The world's been at peace.

143
00:16:57.896 --> 00:16:59.823
Good you are here, Lothar.

144
00:16:59.848 --> 00:17:01.409
It would do the Guardian
a world of good

145
00:17:01.434 --> 00:17:04.527
to see a friendly face
beyond this old one.

146
00:17:05.985 --> 00:17:09.898
He can't refuse you...
nor King Wrynn.

147
00:17:10.165 --> 00:17:12.204
Not if he's summoned.

148
00:17:14.113 --> 00:17:15.527
Chop chop.

149
00:17:46.326 --> 00:17:48.945
Did you summon him, Moroes?

150
00:17:48.970 --> 00:17:52.327
No.
He did not.

151
00:17:57.696 --> 00:18:02.675
So.
You become a sculptor?

152
00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:04.973
I'm making a golem.

153
00:18:05.583 --> 00:18:10.146
It usually takes years of magic
to sip into the clay, but up here it's...

154
00:18:10.171 --> 00:18:12.026
... much faster.

155
00:18:13.885 --> 00:18:19.088
Makes someone to keep Moroes company.
Help to clean up around the house.

156
00:18:19.641 --> 00:18:21.301
Thank you.

157
00:18:25.021 --> 00:18:27.427
It's good to see you, Lothar.

158
00:18:27.452 --> 00:18:30.350
We need your guidance, Medivh.

159
00:18:31.316 --> 00:18:33.606
Our king summons you.

160
00:18:34.828 --> 00:18:37.055
Who's the boy downstairs?

161
00:18:44.948 --> 00:18:46.592
Hello?

162
00:18:48.205 --> 00:18:49.821
Guardian?

163
00:19:42.905 --> 00:19:44.905
Have a good look around?

164
00:19:49.584 --> 00:19:52.728
Getting some ideas what you are going to
do with the place once it's yours?

165
00:19:52.753 --> 00:19:56.460
Guardian, I've renounced my vow.

166
00:19:58.685 --> 00:20:02.133
I didn't want to come here.
I swear, Guardian.

167
00:20:02.158 --> 00:20:04.623
I urged them to find you.
I told them...

168
00:20:04.648 --> 00:20:06.576
... you should be
the one to explain.

169
00:20:06.601 --> 00:20:08.033
Explain what?

170
00:20:08.058 --> 00:20:09.617
Fel !

171
00:20:13.606 --> 00:20:15.337
In Azeroth?

172
00:20:15.362 --> 00:20:17.511
In the barracks,
one of the bodies.

173
00:20:17.536 --> 00:20:19.913
Guardian, what is the fel?

174
00:20:21.141 --> 00:20:25.774
A magic unlike any other.
It feeds on life itself.

175
00:20:25.799 --> 00:20:29.297
It pollutes the user,
twisting everything it touches.

176
00:20:29.322 --> 00:20:33.936
It promises great power but
it exacts a terrible price.

177
00:20:34.288 --> 00:20:37.320
There is no place for
the fel in Azeroth.

178
00:20:38.877 --> 00:20:40.908
You've done the right thing.

179
00:20:42.226 --> 00:20:43.717
We'll go.

180
00:20:53.749 --> 00:20:56.455
Hey.
Go home, you.

181
00:21:04.476 --> 00:21:06.183
Step in.

182
00:21:21.659 --> 00:21:24.907
- Medivh.
- Your Grace.

183
00:21:25.594 --> 00:21:27.620
It has been too long.

184
00:21:30.209 --> 00:21:31.623
Come.

185
00:21:31.648 --> 00:21:34.402
Help us get to the roots
of these troubles about.

186
00:21:37.428 --> 00:21:41.325
- What kind of beasts?
- They are saying giants.

187
00:21:41.350 --> 00:21:43.898
Armed giants.
Wolves to carry them.

188
00:21:43.923 --> 00:21:45.569
Huge unstoppable monsters

189
00:21:45.593 --> 00:21:48.950
What are the other kingdoms?
Are they suffering the same?

190
00:21:48.975 --> 00:21:52.632
All seek our protection yet not trust
us enough to tell us anything.

191
00:21:52.657 --> 00:21:55.967
We know nothing about
these so call monsters.

192
00:21:55.992 --> 00:21:57.638
We need prisoners.

193
00:21:57.663 --> 00:22:00.182
Even a corpse
can tell us something.

194
00:22:01.701 --> 00:22:04.358
I don't know what danger
we're in, Medivh.

195
00:22:04.542 --> 00:22:07.399
I exist to protect this realm, my lord.

196
00:22:07.661 --> 00:22:09.901
It is my very purpose.

197
00:22:09.926 --> 00:22:11.826
I am the Guardian.

198
00:22:11.851 --> 00:22:14.330
At least for the time being anyhow.

199
00:22:15.414 --> 00:22:16.873
Yes.

200
00:22:17.022 --> 00:22:20.796
What are we going to do about...
What is his name?

201
00:22:20.821 --> 00:22:22.825
Khadgar, sire.

202
00:22:24.330 --> 00:22:26.238
He'll be coming with us.

203
00:22:28.952 --> 00:22:30.618
Well then.

204
00:22:31.583 --> 00:22:33.211
We better get going.

205
00:22:33.799 --> 00:22:36.308
ELWYNN
FOREST

206
00:23:03.207 --> 00:23:04.493
Halt!

207
00:23:36.942 --> 00:23:38.785
It can't be.

208
00:23:38.810 --> 00:23:41.679
- What is this?
- Can't tell from the look of it.

209
00:23:42.813 --> 00:23:44.292
.

210
00:23:44.317 --> 00:23:45.720
Guardian.

211
00:23:47.016 --> 00:23:48.611
Close ranks!

212
00:23:48.636 --> 00:23:50.401
Watch your back!

213
00:23:50.800 --> 00:23:53.704
Victory or death!

214
00:24:00.035 --> 00:24:02.261
Watch the flank to your left!

215
00:24:10.799 --> 00:24:12.572
Watch your flank!

216
00:24:15.959 --> 00:24:18.361
- Watch your flank!
- To your left!

217
00:24:27.708 --> 00:24:29.498
Guardian!

218
00:24:48.467 --> 00:24:50.891
Now you die, you beast!

219
00:24:57.661 --> 00:25:00.187
Don't try and take them on
with brute force.

220
00:25:02.184 --> 00:25:04.866
They are stronger.
Be smarter.

221
00:25:44.336 --> 00:25:45.996
The fel.

222
00:25:46.133 --> 00:25:47.972
They're all dying.

223
00:25:48.181 --> 00:25:50.179
Only the green ones!

224
00:25:50.204 --> 00:25:52.363
Kill that big bastard!

225
00:25:59.448 --> 00:26:02.284
Durotan.
Move.

226
00:26:13.571 --> 00:26:17.142
Guardian.
Guardian, what did you do?

227
00:26:17.675 --> 00:26:19.575
I was right, wasn't I?
It's here.

228
00:26:19.600 --> 00:26:23.074
- Where are you going?
- Get these men safely back to Stormwind.

229
00:26:23.099 --> 00:26:25.354
I've to return to Karazhan.

230
00:26:26.222 --> 00:26:28.187
You did well today.

231
00:26:31.734 --> 00:26:34.252
- Where's the Guardian?
- Karazhan.

232
00:26:34.331 --> 00:26:36.383
We need a prisoner.
Where's your horse?

233
00:26:36.408 --> 00:26:38.513
- Uh. They took my horse.
- Really?

234
00:26:38.537 --> 00:26:40.691
Just stay there.

235
00:28:23.999 --> 00:28:26.341
How much do you
love your master?

236
00:28:27.502 --> 00:28:29.053
I'll do it.

237
00:28:30.885 --> 00:28:32.472
Back off!

238
00:28:36.849 --> 00:28:40.876
Pity.
It would have make a good coat.

239
00:28:56.966 --> 00:28:58.993
Over here!

240
00:29:08.722 --> 00:29:11.517
- You took it alone.
- Yes.

241
00:29:12.492 --> 00:29:14.768
Looks like the runt to the litter.

242
00:29:28.198 --> 00:29:30.353
You.
What are you?

243
00:29:30.378 --> 00:29:32.870
And why do you
attack our lands?

244
00:29:34.827 --> 00:29:38.762
- He does not know what you speak.
- You speak our language?

245
00:29:38.787 --> 00:29:41.002
Speak one more word
in their language.

246
00:29:41.027 --> 00:29:44.074
And I will wear your tongue.

247
00:29:55.044 --> 00:29:57.750
I will not warn you again.

248
00:30:02.148 --> 00:30:04.560
- Tell him to stop.
- You tell him.

249
00:30:11.597 --> 00:30:13.245
You're welcome.

250
00:30:16.798 --> 00:30:18.753
Have you a name?

251
00:30:21.543 --> 00:30:23.898
You understand our language.

252
00:30:25.868 --> 00:30:29.506
Again, have you a name?

253
00:30:35.081 --> 00:30:36.849
Garona.

254
00:30:37.658 --> 00:30:40.277
She calls herself, Garona.

255
00:30:41.992 --> 00:30:43.970
What kind of being are you?

256
00:30:43.995 --> 00:30:47.339
She seems more like us
than those... beast we fought.

257
00:30:47.370 --> 00:30:48.602
Orc.

258
00:30:48.627 --> 00:30:50.070
Orc?

259
00:30:50.095 --> 00:30:53.465
That's what you are?
Or the beast in the cage was?

260
00:30:55.579 --> 00:30:59.325
I know every races in the Seven Kingdoms.
I've never heard of orc.

261
00:31:01.663 --> 00:31:03.755
Show me where you come from.

262
00:31:09.312 --> 00:31:11.485
This is not orc world.

263
00:31:11.787 --> 00:31:13.793
Orc world is dead.

264
00:31:14.293 --> 00:31:16.361
Orcs take this world now.

265
00:31:16.386 --> 00:31:18.595
Not from this world.

266
00:31:18.621 --> 00:31:21.107
How did you get here?

267
00:31:22.309 --> 00:31:23.988
The great gate.

268
00:31:24.013 --> 00:31:26.918
Deep in ground and through
magic brought us here.

269
00:31:26.943 --> 00:31:29.416
But how did you learn our language?

270
00:31:29.441 --> 00:31:31.203
Orc take prisoner for the gate.

271
00:31:31.228 --> 00:31:33.241
- I learn from them.
- Prisoners?

272
00:31:33.266 --> 00:31:36.713
Our people?
Are they alive?

273
00:31:36.738 --> 00:31:38.003
Yes.

274
00:31:38.028 --> 00:31:39.873
- Many.
- Why?

275
00:31:39.898 --> 00:31:41.772
To feed the gate.

276
00:31:41.797 --> 00:31:45.040
To bring the Horde
to take your world.

277
00:31:45.065 --> 00:31:46.832
You'll take us to them.

278
00:31:47.553 --> 00:31:48.777
No.

279
00:31:48.802 --> 00:31:53.804
You'll take us to them or you will
end up like your friend in the cage.

280
00:31:57.882 --> 00:32:00.086
You think you are fearsome.

281
00:32:01.240 --> 00:32:03.474
Orc children have pets
more fearsome than you.

282
00:32:03.499 --> 00:32:06.072
We're not trying to be fearsome, Garona.

283
00:32:06.097 --> 00:32:09.534
We are trying to protect
our people, our families.

284
00:32:09.559 --> 00:32:12.991
If you help us.
I give you my oath.

285
00:32:13.210 --> 00:32:15.159
You will have your freedom.

286
00:32:19.725 --> 00:32:22.395
Fearsome Blackhand.

287
00:32:22.893 --> 00:32:25.859
Warchief of the Horde.

288
00:32:26.215 --> 00:32:31.650
You have allowed the smallteeths
to kill your warriors.

289
00:32:32.074 --> 00:32:33.150
Worse.

290
00:32:33.175 --> 00:32:37.284
You shamed your people
by running from an enemy.

291
00:32:38.607 --> 00:32:42.056
Are you too weak
to talk, destroyer?

292
00:32:42.081 --> 00:32:45.574
The Horde has no use
for weakness.

293
00:32:45.599 --> 00:32:48.974
Respect our tradition, warchief.

294
00:32:52.168 --> 00:32:54.675
You know the penalty.

295
00:32:56.420 --> 00:32:58.134
Death.

296
00:33:15.602 --> 00:33:16.911
Done.

297
00:33:19.577 --> 00:33:24.784
- You dare interrupt this judgment?
- We fought hard!

298
00:33:25.209 --> 00:33:28.324
Their warlock use
your fel against us.

299
00:33:28.363 --> 00:33:31.246
Only I can control the fel!

300
00:33:35.502 --> 00:33:38.809
I see you and
your men have survived.

301
00:33:38.834 --> 00:33:43.822
Perhaps Blackhand kept you
safely away from the battlefield.

302
00:33:44.184 --> 00:33:47.507
Maybe he knows you are weak too.

303
00:33:49.011 --> 00:33:53.359
Do you wish to challenge me,
little chieftain.

304
00:33:57.725 --> 00:33:59.992
I do not question, Gul'dan.

305
00:34:00.017 --> 00:34:04.834
But the fel is born of death,
must have a price.

306
00:34:06.386 --> 00:34:09.549
A price paid in lives taken.

307
00:34:21.810 --> 00:34:23.944
Will you hold your son?

308
00:34:39.442 --> 00:34:42.038
He will be a great chieftain.

309
00:34:42.063 --> 00:34:45.860
Like his father,
a born leader.

310
00:34:45.885 --> 00:34:48.407
I was no leader today.

311
00:34:56.094 --> 00:34:58.723
He challenges you already.

312
00:34:59.798 --> 00:35:03.552
If Gul'dan can infect
born as innocent as he.

313
00:35:03.687 --> 00:35:06.422
What chance do
the rest of us have?

314
00:35:09.652 --> 00:35:12.244
Whatever happens.

315
00:35:12.524 --> 00:35:14.457
Whatever happens.

316
00:35:27.606 --> 00:35:29.404
I see you.

317
00:35:30.446 --> 00:35:34.688
This gate,
who showed it to Gul'dan?

318
00:35:34.948 --> 00:35:37.379
Who lead him to Azeroth?

319
00:35:37.667 --> 00:35:39.965
Gul'dan call him a demon.

320
00:35:39.990 --> 00:35:41.719
Did you see it?

321
00:35:42.021 --> 00:35:45.522
Not the face,
but the voice...

322
00:35:45.928 --> 00:35:48.185
Like fire and ash.

323
00:36:04.111 --> 00:36:06.382
I'll be here if you need me.

324
00:36:22.600 --> 00:36:24.148
Your mate.

325
00:36:24.385 --> 00:36:26.936
I could kill you before
he even reaches me.

326
00:36:29.557 --> 00:36:31.182
Lothar?

327
00:36:32.172 --> 00:36:34.218
He is my brother.

328
00:36:34.608 --> 00:36:37.169
The king is my mate.

329
00:36:38.201 --> 00:36:40.326
You are the chieftain's wife then?

330
00:36:40.351 --> 00:36:42.316
I suppose so.

331
00:36:44.100 --> 00:36:46.426
Then killing you will bring
me even greater honor.

332
00:36:46.451 --> 00:36:48.329
Not among my kind.

333
00:36:49.499 --> 00:36:51.437
It is a cold night.

334
00:36:51.642 --> 00:36:53.944
I thought you might use these.

335
00:37:04.209 --> 00:37:06.113
It will warm you.

336
00:37:14.866 --> 00:37:17.479
More of our villages burned tonight.

337
00:37:19.484 --> 00:37:21.952
One of them is
the village of my birth.

338
00:37:24.890 --> 00:37:28.183
I can not imagine what horrors
you have been through, Garona.

339
00:37:28.841 --> 00:37:31.532
But this does not
need to happen.

340
00:37:31.558 --> 00:37:34.950
We have peace in these lands
for many years now.

341
00:37:34.975 --> 00:37:38.220
Peace between races
from all over the world.

342
00:37:44.002 --> 00:37:45.632
What is this?

343
00:37:49.897 --> 00:37:52.117
I can have it removed.

344
00:37:54.968 --> 00:37:57.259
There is a life here
for you, Garona.

345
00:37:57.284 --> 00:38:01.360
With us.
A life of freedom.

346
00:38:02.442 --> 00:38:04.225
If you want it.

347
00:38:16.312 --> 00:38:18.420
The great gate.

348
00:38:25.488 --> 00:38:31.889
From light comes darkness
and from darkness, light.

349
00:38:31.965 --> 00:38:33.823
Well, that's clear.

350
00:38:34.074 --> 00:38:36.288
Ask Alodi.

351
00:38:36.313 --> 00:38:38.170
Alodi.

352
00:38:52.323 --> 00:38:55.031
Ahh.
It's good to see trees again.

353
00:38:55.572 --> 00:38:57.455
And the snow.

354
00:38:57.828 --> 00:38:59.799
Even from a distance.

355
00:39:01.253 --> 00:39:05.315
Remember when we would track
blood ox through the Frostwind dunes?

356
00:39:05.390 --> 00:39:09.386
There was always meat.
Always life.

357
00:39:09.870 --> 00:39:11.593
You don't think it's strange

358
00:39:11.618 --> 00:39:14.692
that we lost our home when
Gul'dan came to power.

359
00:39:14.717 --> 00:39:17.225
One orc could not
kill a world, Durotan.

360
00:39:17.250 --> 00:39:19.028
Are you sure?

361
00:39:19.217 --> 00:39:23.715
Look around you.
Does it not remind you of something?

362
00:39:25.710 --> 00:39:29.846
Wherever Gul'dan works his magic,
the land dies.

363
00:39:30.383 --> 00:39:35.019
If our people are to make
a home here, my friend.

364
00:39:37.271 --> 00:39:39.537
Gul'dan must be stopped.

365
00:39:41.528 --> 00:39:44.237
We are not powerful
enough to defeat Gul'dan.

366
00:39:44.262 --> 00:39:45.609
No.

367
00:39:47.321 --> 00:39:48.621
No.

368
00:39:52.178 --> 00:39:56.555
But with the humans help,
we could be.

369
00:40:10.382 --> 00:40:12.369
I want that weapon.

370
00:40:16.084 --> 00:40:17.968
You'll have me to protect you.

371
00:40:17.993 --> 00:40:20.266
I need no one
to protect me.

372
00:40:26.493 --> 00:40:28.233
What are you looking at?

373
00:41:06.378 --> 00:41:08.850
Bookworm.
Take the first watch.

374
00:41:08.875 --> 00:41:11.637
Respectfully, Commander,
my name is Khadgar.

375
00:41:11.662 --> 00:41:14.380
My deepest apologies, Khadgar.

376
00:41:14.405 --> 00:41:16.365
You see, I thought
we bonded when

377
00:41:16.390 --> 00:41:19.678
I didn't put you in a prison cell
for breaking into royal barracks.

378
00:41:20.623 --> 00:41:22.477
Now take the watch.

379
00:41:36.012 --> 00:41:39.807
Well.
At least you're not reading.

380
00:41:43.120 --> 00:41:45.296
He wishes to lie with me.

381
00:41:47.456 --> 00:41:49.275
I beg your pardon?

382
00:41:50.085 --> 00:41:51.997
You will be injured

383
00:41:52.212 --> 00:41:54.912
- I don't want to lie with you.
- Good.

384
00:41:54.937 --> 00:41:57.212
You would not be
an effective mate.

385
00:41:58.048 --> 00:41:59.740
Why do you laugh?

386
00:42:00.528 --> 00:42:03.377
I can't see how you humans
survive such a thing.

387
00:42:03.402 --> 00:42:07.294
No muscles to protect you.
Brittle bones that break.

388
00:42:07.319 --> 00:42:09.687
You don't look that
different to us.

389
00:42:10.139 --> 00:42:12.143
How did you survive?

390
00:42:12.168 --> 00:42:14.729
Broken bones heal stronger.

391
00:42:15.336 --> 00:42:17.550
Mine are very strong.

392
00:42:21.228 --> 00:42:22.739
I'm sorry.

393
00:42:22.925 --> 00:42:24.738
Do not be.

394
00:42:28.810 --> 00:42:32.670
My name, Garona,

395
00:42:33.694 --> 00:42:35.849
it means "cursed" in orc.

396
00:42:40.381 --> 00:42:43.513
My mother was burned alive
for giving birth to me.

397
00:42:48.790 --> 00:42:50.910
They kept you alive though.

398
00:42:51.499 --> 00:42:53.072
Gul'dan did.

399
00:42:56.010 --> 00:43:01.546
He gave me her tusk
to remember her.

400
00:43:09.276 --> 00:43:13.210
My parents gave me to the Kirin Tor
when I was 6 years old.

401
00:43:14.531 --> 00:43:20.738
That's the last time I saw them or...
any of my brothers and sisters.

402
00:43:23.199 --> 00:43:27.654
It brings a family honor
to offer a child to the Kirin Tor.

403
00:43:28.008 --> 00:43:30.928
To have their son taken up
to the floating city of Dalaran

404
00:43:30.953 --> 00:43:34.595
and be trained by the most
powerful mages in the land.

405
00:43:36.347 --> 00:43:39.231
Less so,
to have them run away.

406
00:43:43.302 --> 00:43:47.829
Well.
That was cheerful.

407
00:43:50.622 --> 00:43:52.485
The great gate.

408
00:43:55.407 --> 00:43:58.189
Why do they need
so many prisoners?

409
00:43:58.404 --> 00:44:00.638
Like wood for a fire.

410
00:44:00.890 --> 00:44:03.688
Green magic takes life
to open the gate.

411
00:44:04.189 --> 00:44:06.348
How many more orcs are
they planning on bringing?

412
00:44:06.373 --> 00:44:09.926
All of them.
This is just a warband.

413
00:44:10.331 --> 00:44:14.708
When the portal is open,
Gul'dan will bring the Horde.

414
00:44:21.913 --> 00:44:23.965
Get them back to Stormwind.

415
00:44:24.462 --> 00:44:26.199
We ride ahead.

416
00:44:36.233 --> 00:44:39.729
Garona, we should go.
It's not safe...

417
00:44:40.885 --> 00:44:42.258
Durotan.

418
00:44:42.283 --> 00:44:46.464
To the north, there is a black rock
that touches the sky.

419
00:44:47.057 --> 00:44:49.188
I would meet with their leader.

420
00:44:49.213 --> 00:44:51.003
To challenge him?

421
00:44:51.028 --> 00:44:54.326
I saw you, lead the smallteeths
to our encampment.

422
00:44:54.351 --> 00:44:57.172
They have seen
what is being built.

423
00:44:57.326 --> 00:45:01.692
And only you know, what
Gul'dan has planned for my people.

424
00:45:01.717 --> 00:45:06.499
His magic is death
to all things.

425
00:45:07.958 --> 00:45:09.869
He must be stopped.

426
00:45:11.533 --> 00:45:16.899
Tell him, the black rock,
when the sun is highest.

427
00:45:16.950 --> 00:45:18.562
I will.

428
00:45:20.069 --> 00:45:21.564
Chieftain.

429
00:45:22.188 --> 00:45:26.622
If I returned, would you
take me into your clan?

430
00:45:28.676 --> 00:45:32.504
You're safer here,
with them.

431
00:46:24.002 --> 00:46:25.978
Is it as you feared?

432
00:46:26.003 --> 00:46:30.848
- The fel is everywhere.
- Then you mustn't leave again.

433
00:46:32.559 --> 00:46:35.839
They need the Guardian's help
now more than ever.

434
00:46:36.935 --> 00:46:39.380
Maybe the boy can help.

435
00:46:44.738 --> 00:46:47.108
- We need solution!
- Easy for you to say!

436
00:46:47.133 --> 00:46:52.232
- The Dwarf enforgers must work overtime.
- You treat us no better than dogs.

437
00:46:52.257 --> 00:46:55.945
- We shall supply you no more!
- Enough!

438
00:46:57.042 --> 00:47:01.431
You have all called on Stormwind in
the past either for troops or arbitration.

439
00:47:02.154 --> 00:47:08.010
If we do not unite to fight
this enemy, we will perish.

440
00:47:08.035 --> 00:47:11.490
Stormwind needs soldiers,
arms, horses...

441
00:47:11.515 --> 00:47:13.844
Ha! We have our own
kingdoms to look after.

442
00:47:13.869 --> 00:47:16.667
- Fight your own wars!
- Your Majesty.

443
00:47:17.302 --> 00:47:18.318
Commander.

444
00:47:18.343 --> 00:47:22.221
The Orcs are building a portal, through
which they plan to bring an army.

445
00:47:22.246 --> 00:47:25.915
If we do not stop them now,
we may never get another opportunity.

446
00:47:25.940 --> 00:47:30.090
Where is he?
Where is the protector of Azeroth?

447
00:47:30.115 --> 00:47:31.399
Where the Guardian?

448
00:47:31.424 --> 00:47:33.193
Where is Medivh?

449
00:47:33.704 --> 00:47:35.458
- My liege.
- I suggest we take a recess.

450
00:47:35.483 --> 00:47:39.377
Take as long as you like.
We're done.

451
00:47:43.208 --> 00:47:44.874
Commander.

452
00:47:44.899 --> 00:47:47.574
What's left of the 4th
has retreated from Stonewatch.

453
00:47:47.599 --> 00:47:49.378
What's left?

454
00:47:49.403 --> 00:47:51.989
Callan is among the injured.

455
00:47:58.455 --> 00:47:59.977
Dad?

456
00:48:05.874 --> 00:48:07.764
I'm fine.
It's fine.

457
00:48:10.554 --> 00:48:12.365
You had me worried.

458
00:48:16.132 --> 00:48:18.159
Where's the rest of your troop?

459
00:48:18.184 --> 00:48:20.660
They took most of them alive.

460
00:48:21.250 --> 00:48:23.198
We'll get them back.

461
00:48:24.054 --> 00:48:26.136
Don't be in such a hurry.

462
00:48:31.749 --> 00:48:33.646
You're all I have.

463
00:48:35.606 --> 00:48:39.033
I know.
I'm a soldier.

464
00:48:48.222 --> 00:48:52.599
He would not ask for this meeting if
he thought he could defeat Gul'dan alone.

465
00:48:54.549 --> 00:48:57.753
- The fel must truly terrified him.
- Durotan is scared of nothing.

466
00:48:57.778 --> 00:48:59.854
The location.

467
00:49:01.122 --> 00:49:03.746
The suddenness of this meeting.

468
00:49:04.986 --> 00:49:06.928
- Sounds like a trap.
- It is not.

469
00:49:06.953 --> 00:49:08.469
- Could be.
- It is not.

470
00:49:08.494 --> 00:49:10.253
- Could be.
- It is not.

471
00:49:10.278 --> 00:49:11.953
What do you think?

472
00:49:12.316 --> 00:49:14.689
It's too good an
opportunity to ignore.

473
00:49:14.714 --> 00:49:17.163
I think we have no choice.

474
00:49:17.952 --> 00:49:21.085
We must stop the orcs
from opening the portal.

475
00:49:21.923 --> 00:49:23.900
But we will need help.

476
00:49:23.925 --> 00:49:26.102
- And if he's lying?
- Orcs do not lie.

477
00:49:26.127 --> 00:49:28.371
- What if he is?
- There is no honor in it.

478
00:49:28.396 --> 00:49:31.700
And where's the 'honor'
in him betraying his own people?

479
00:49:31.725 --> 00:49:35.555
Durotan is protecting his clan.
His enemy is the fel.

480
00:49:35.580 --> 00:49:37.642
Gul'dan is the betrayer.

481
00:49:37.667 --> 00:49:41.517
This orc, Durotan.
How do you know him?

482
00:49:41.542 --> 00:49:45.208
He freed me,
and he is loved by his clan.

483
00:49:45.552 --> 00:49:47.852
He's a strong chieftain.

484
00:49:47.877 --> 00:49:51.095
Strong chiefs must earn
their clans trust.

485
00:49:51.818 --> 00:49:54.432
If we are to expect you
to join us.

486
00:49:55.654 --> 00:49:57.732
We must earn yours.

487
00:50:05.705 --> 00:50:07.812
To defend yourself.

488
00:50:09.408 --> 00:50:10.835
With this?

489
00:50:10.860 --> 00:50:12.456
Yes.

490
00:50:14.092 --> 00:50:15.868
Find the Guardian.

491
00:50:18.603 --> 00:50:20.449
What is this?

492
00:50:21.127 --> 00:50:22.694
Guardian?

493
00:50:24.381 --> 00:50:25.668
Uh.

494
00:50:26.552 --> 00:50:29.346
The gate.
We saw it, in the morass.

495
00:50:29.371 --> 00:50:31.974
I've been putting together
all the clues I can about it.

496
00:50:31.999 --> 00:50:34.708
This.
This drawing.

497
00:50:34.733 --> 00:50:36.990
- Where did you copy it from?
- Guardian.

498
00:50:37.015 --> 00:50:38.620
And this?

499
00:50:41.351 --> 00:50:44.543
And this?
And this?

500
00:50:44.568 --> 00:50:47.131
I've been researching ever since
I felt the presence of the fel.

501
00:50:47.156 --> 00:50:51.757
I am the Guardian.
Me, not you.

502
00:50:51.902 --> 00:50:53.517
Not yet.

503
00:50:53.542 --> 00:50:55.995
I just thought you might
appreciate some help.

504
00:51:04.937 --> 00:51:08.128
Don't presume you can help me.

505
00:51:08.153 --> 00:51:13.665
You have no idea the forces
I contend with.

506
00:51:14.558 --> 00:51:20.076
If you want to help,
protect the king.

507
00:51:20.590 --> 00:51:22.735
You leave the fel to me.

508
00:51:34.530 --> 00:51:37.570
- Interesting choice.
- Guardian.

509
00:51:40.999 --> 00:51:43.793
Pack up and move
to the west gate.

510
00:51:48.339 --> 00:51:49.422
You there.

511
00:51:49.448 --> 00:51:51.934
Pack up your stall
and get moving now!

512
00:51:58.240 --> 00:51:59.525
I need your help.

513
00:51:59.550 --> 00:52:01.802
- I found a book.
- Of course you did.

514
00:52:01.827 --> 00:52:03.577
There was an illustration
that showed the gate

515
00:52:03.602 --> 00:52:05.644
like the one
we saw being built.

516
00:52:06.246 --> 00:52:08.520
- Sorry. Sorry.
- Khadgar.

517
00:52:09.977 --> 00:52:12.744
Listen. I tried to show the Guardian
but he became furious.

518
00:52:12.769 --> 00:52:14.671
He burned all my research.

519
00:52:14.696 --> 00:52:17.604
He would have burn this too
If I hadn't hidden it in my robe.

520
00:52:24.130 --> 00:52:26.711
No, turn the page.
Here.

521
00:52:27.309 --> 00:52:28.756
Look.

522
00:52:28.781 --> 00:52:30.272
See.

523
00:52:33.519 --> 00:52:34.875
What do you think
the image means?

524
00:52:34.900 --> 00:52:36.829
The orcs were summoned.

525
00:52:36.854 --> 00:52:39.785
From this side of the gate.
They were invited in.

526
00:52:44.370 --> 00:52:47.011
And the Guardian
burned your research.

527
00:52:49.624 --> 00:52:52.116
He's probably just
trying to protect you.

528
00:52:53.690 --> 00:52:55.331
Now go away.

529
00:53:12.498 --> 00:53:15.261
Good spot for an ambush.

530
00:53:17.183 --> 00:53:19.611
Our sentries are well placed.

531
00:53:21.339 --> 00:53:23.296
I will check again.

532
00:54:20.960 --> 00:54:23.538
You asked to speak
with the humanking.

533
00:54:23.563 --> 00:54:25.177
Here he stands.

534
00:54:27.618 --> 00:54:29.387
I am the King Llane.

535
00:54:29.933 --> 00:54:32.396
I'm told you wished to talk.

536
00:54:38.019 --> 00:54:41.088
Ask him if they plan
to return to their home?

537
00:54:50.038 --> 00:54:52.113
Our world is destroyed.

538
00:54:53.895 --> 00:54:55.392
There is nothing to go back to.

539
00:54:55.417 --> 00:54:58.852
We are not responsible
for destroying your world.

540
00:54:59.602 --> 00:55:02.005
War with us will solve nothing.

541
00:55:08.457 --> 00:55:12.145
He says,
"Orcs, war solves everything."

542
00:55:13.067 --> 00:55:15.068
Then why is he here?

543
00:55:19.420 --> 00:55:21.661
To save my people.

544
00:55:23.105 --> 00:55:26.601
Fel takes life from
more than it's victims.

545
00:55:27.910 --> 00:55:31.095
Kills the earth and
corrupts those who use it.

546
00:55:32.093 --> 00:55:35.610
Gul'dan will poison everything
with his death magic.

547
00:55:36.030 --> 00:55:41.341
If my people are to survive,
Gul'dan must be destroyed.

548
00:55:43.615 --> 00:55:47.944
In 2 suns, the humans
we have captured...

549
00:55:49.447 --> 00:55:51.984
... be used to fuel the portal.

550
00:55:52.412 --> 00:55:57.041
If you attack our camp,
and draw his warriors away,

551
00:55:58.712 --> 00:56:02.480
Frostwolf clan,
will kill him.

552
00:56:04.400 --> 00:56:06.407
Two days.

553
00:56:08.620 --> 00:56:13.798
If we do this,
you will protect my people until then.

554
00:56:16.689 --> 00:56:18.569
I will try.

555
00:56:22.495 --> 00:56:24.075
It's a trap!

556
00:56:24.100 --> 00:56:25.988
Traitor die!

557
00:56:29.606 --> 00:56:30.675
Retreat!

558
00:56:30.700 --> 00:56:33.533
Back!
Return to our camp!

559
00:56:34.253 --> 00:56:36.257
Fall back!

560
00:57:04.089 --> 00:57:05.972
Stay together!

561
00:57:10.087 --> 00:57:12.547
Focus.
Like old times.

562
00:57:23.111 --> 00:57:25.747
Cover your flank!

563
00:57:32.278 --> 00:57:33.942
Spread out!

564
00:57:36.181 --> 00:57:38.157
Swords!

565
00:57:52.461 --> 00:57:54.030
You alright?

566
00:57:56.486 --> 00:57:58.816
You are no good to us dead.
Go.

567
00:57:58.841 --> 00:58:00.588
I'll get the others.

568
00:58:01.461 --> 00:58:02.480
Fall back!

569
00:58:02.505 --> 00:58:04.446
We're all getting out.

570
00:58:04.471 --> 00:58:06.721
Medivh will cover our retreat.

571
00:58:06.746 --> 00:58:08.478
Fall back!

572
00:58:19.572 --> 00:58:21.348
Garona!

573
00:58:23.549 --> 00:58:25.376
Stay together!

574
00:58:28.849 --> 00:58:30.628
Fall back!

575
00:58:32.049 --> 00:58:34.240
Go on, now!

576
00:58:34.265 --> 00:58:36.560
Where's the bloody Guardian?

577
00:58:42.370 --> 00:58:44.627
Protect the king.
I got them.

578
00:58:44.652 --> 00:58:46.865
Move back!

579
00:59:00.814 --> 00:59:05.282
Shield FORMATION !

580
00:59:53.522 --> 00:59:55.690
Retreat to the plateau.

581
00:59:56.131 --> 00:59:57.558
Fall back!

582
00:59:57.583 --> 01:00:00.496
Up the hill.
Move!

583
01:00:19.223 --> 01:00:20.681
Medivh.

584
01:00:24.043 --> 01:00:27.074
Medivh, take it down!

585
01:00:38.739 --> 01:00:40.446
Medivh!

586
01:00:46.176 --> 01:00:48.072
Hold on, son.

587
01:00:50.065 --> 01:00:51.419
Dad.

588
01:00:54.023 --> 01:00:55.800
For Azeroth.

589
01:00:56.768 --> 01:00:58.489
Medivh!

590
01:01:32.357 --> 01:01:33.884
Stop.

591
01:01:35.735 --> 01:01:37.062
No.

592
01:01:39.936 --> 01:01:41.387
Callan.

593
01:02:49.837 --> 01:02:51.289
He's here!

594
01:02:55.292 --> 01:02:56.488
What's wrong with him?

595
01:02:56.513 --> 01:02:57.907
We need to get
him to Karazhan.

596
01:02:57.932 --> 01:03:00.536
- I'll get the horses.
- You won't make any time by road.

597
01:03:00.561 --> 01:03:02.406
Take one of my birds.

598
01:03:11.492 --> 01:03:13.392
Place him in the font.

599
01:03:15.417 --> 01:03:19.349
- Moroes, what's wrong with him
- I told him not to leave Karazhan.

600
01:03:34.161 --> 01:03:35.881
I have to go.

601
01:03:36.744 --> 01:03:39.238
We need the help of
the Karin Tor, now.

602
01:03:39.263 --> 01:03:40.229
Go.

603
01:03:40.254 --> 01:03:43.282
There are medicines I must prepare.
Sit with him.

604
01:03:47.244 --> 01:03:50.176
You and the baby
must leave now.

605
01:03:52.101 --> 01:03:54.845
You're a traitor, Durotan.

606
01:03:55.524 --> 01:03:56.963
No.

607
01:03:56.988 --> 01:04:00.565
One who values what we once were.
Like you used to.

608
01:04:00.590 --> 01:04:02.531
That time is past.

609
01:04:02.556 --> 01:04:05.345
We are but fuel
for the fel now.

610
01:04:05.370 --> 01:04:07.507
There is still hope, Blackhand.

611
01:04:07.532 --> 01:04:09.304
Our children.

612
01:04:18.455 --> 01:04:23.771
Do not make me take more
innocent lives, young chieftain.

613
01:04:26.823 --> 01:04:28.823
If I submit...

614
01:04:30.227 --> 01:04:32.688
... will you let my people be?

615
01:04:42.623 --> 01:04:44.962
What will I call our son?

616
01:04:49.726 --> 01:04:51.345
Go'el

617
01:05:07.577 --> 01:05:09.219
You.

618
01:05:09.317 --> 01:05:11.197
Where's the older man?

619
01:05:11.662 --> 01:05:13.759
He told me to watch you.

620
01:05:15.474 --> 01:05:18.294
- The king.
- He is alive.

621
01:05:20.973 --> 01:05:23.093
Lothar's son is dead.

622
01:05:27.358 --> 01:05:29.609
I argued for the meeting.

623
01:05:31.450 --> 01:05:33.630
Lothar will hate me.

624
01:05:33.748 --> 01:05:35.667
This upsets you.

625
01:05:38.784 --> 01:05:40.869
He is a great warrior.

626
01:05:42.200 --> 01:05:43.989
He defends his people well.

627
01:05:44.014 --> 01:05:47.031
A good mate for an orc.

628
01:05:47.425 --> 01:05:49.355
I am no orc.

629
01:05:51.423 --> 01:05:53.569
I am no human either.

630
01:05:56.514 --> 01:06:01.812
When I was younger,
I used to feel apart from my kin.

631
01:06:01.837 --> 01:06:09.288
I traveled far and wide,
looking for... wisdom.

632
01:06:09.313 --> 01:06:14.763
Feel a connection with all the souls
I was charged with protecting.

633
01:06:15.088 --> 01:06:19.887
On my travel, I met
a strong and noble people.

634
01:06:20.365 --> 01:06:26.238
Among them, a female,
who accepted me for what I was.

635
01:06:26.263 --> 01:06:28.374
Who loved me.

636
01:06:30.830 --> 01:06:33.984
It was not a life
I was fated to have,

637
01:06:34.009 --> 01:06:36.153
but it taught me something.

638
01:06:36.717 --> 01:06:39.264
If love is what you need,

639
01:06:40.447 --> 01:06:44.293
you must be willing to travel
to the end the world to find it.

640
01:06:50.110 --> 01:06:51.851
You left your mate.

641
01:06:51.876 --> 01:06:53.793
Go find Lothar.

642
01:07:15.275 --> 01:07:17.527
Step inside the circle.

643
01:07:26.534 --> 01:07:32.596
This... is my gift to you,
Garona.

644
01:08:02.539 --> 01:08:05.682
A whole world and
exchange for a statue.

645
01:08:06.335 --> 01:08:09.043
Gods are strange creatures.

646
01:08:11.479 --> 01:08:16.659
Frostwolves, you are a practical people.

647
01:08:16.786 --> 01:08:20.918
Those of us from the south have
always admired that about you.

648
01:08:26.840 --> 01:08:32.116
When the portal opens,
when the rest of the Horde join us

649
01:08:32.148 --> 01:08:34.961
we will give them the fel.

650
01:08:35.277 --> 01:08:38.115
- All of them.
- Durotan did not agree to this!

651
01:08:38.140 --> 01:08:41.761
And why would you care
what that traitor thinks?

652
01:08:42.178 --> 01:08:45.777
It is time for a new leader
of the Frostwolf clan.

653
01:08:45.802 --> 01:08:49.206
One who has the best interest
of his orcs in mind.

654
01:08:49.238 --> 01:08:52.879
One who appreciates Gul'dan's vision,

655
01:08:55.479 --> 01:08:57.366
... his power.

656
01:08:58.348 --> 01:08:59.853
Come.

657
01:09:00.644 --> 01:09:03.275
I will grant you the fel.

658
01:09:04.613 --> 01:09:10.200
Durotan, he... has poisoned
the Frostwolves against the fel.

659
01:09:10.427 --> 01:09:14.544
Let me gather them,
bring them here.

660
01:09:15.179 --> 01:09:18.132
Grant me the fel in front of them,
let them see...

661
01:09:18.157 --> 01:09:20.979
How much stronger I become.

662
01:09:22.120 --> 01:09:26.515
As I said,
a practical people.

663
01:09:27.675 --> 01:09:29.980
This is a new dawn.

664
01:09:30.005 --> 01:09:32.808
The time of the Horde.

665
01:09:33.316 --> 01:09:38.326
Be feared,
or be fuel.

666
01:09:50.986 --> 01:09:52.749
I'm sorry.

667
01:09:54.980 --> 01:09:56.998
Callan's mother,

668
01:09:58.524 --> 01:10:00.841
died in childbirth.

669
01:10:04.592 --> 01:10:08.309
I blamed him for it,
for years.

670
01:10:08.969 --> 01:10:11.156
I'm not going to blame you.

671
01:10:20.920 --> 01:10:22.843
He was so young.

672
01:10:34.504 --> 01:10:36.715
In my entire life,

673
01:10:39.301 --> 01:10:43.615
I have never felt
so much pain as I do now.

674
01:10:59.706 --> 01:11:03.071
Gul'dan does not want to waste
his power on the Frostwolves.

675
01:11:03.096 --> 01:11:04.986
Burn them!

676
01:11:10.273 --> 01:11:13.387
Take the weak,
kill the strong!

677
01:11:29.608 --> 01:11:32.181
I'll bathe in your blood.

678
01:11:32.206 --> 01:11:34.637
Maybe, but not now.

679
01:11:34.662 --> 01:11:38.976
I can't give you long,
but I can give you a head start.

680
01:11:40.636 --> 01:11:43.377
For the sake of your son, Draka.

681
01:11:43.402 --> 01:11:46.762
Leave... now.

682
01:12:01.124 --> 01:12:05.989
You should have trusted in your
chieftain, Orgrim Doomhammer.

683
01:12:43.814 --> 01:12:45.403
Wait for me.

684
01:12:45.956 --> 01:12:48.837
- Khadgar!
- How dare you to come here!

685
01:12:48.862 --> 01:12:49.769
Get out!

686
01:12:49.794 --> 01:12:51.311
I come seeking your wisdom.

687
01:12:51.336 --> 01:12:53.169
There is nothing
for you here now.

688
01:12:53.194 --> 01:12:55.602
The Guardian, Medivh, is unwell.

689
01:12:55.627 --> 01:12:56.678
What?

690
01:12:56.703 --> 01:12:58.745
- He's been poisoned by the fel.
- What?

691
01:12:58.770 --> 01:13:00.832
Ridiculous.

692
01:13:00.857 --> 01:13:02.654
What do you know
of the dark portal?

693
01:13:02.679 --> 01:13:05.548
You come back,
and accused the Guardian...

694
01:13:05.573 --> 01:13:07.247
What is Alodi?

695
01:13:07.272 --> 01:13:09.186
How does he know?

696
01:13:16.137 --> 01:13:17.784
Alodi.

697
01:13:18.282 --> 01:13:19.756
What is it?

698
01:13:19.962 --> 01:13:23.967
An entity from a time
before the Kirin Tor existed.

699
01:13:24.204 --> 01:13:27.805
We think it serve the functions
similar to that of the Guardian.

700
01:13:27.830 --> 01:13:29.434
Protector.

701
01:13:30.093 --> 01:13:35.196
No one beyond the arch council knows
of it's existence, and it will stay that way.

702
01:13:35.566 --> 01:13:37.548
And you to mention it
in the same breath

703
01:13:37.573 --> 01:13:40.586
as the dark portal is
too much to be mere...

704
01:13:43.804 --> 01:13:45.627
... coincidence.

705
01:13:47.506 --> 01:13:49.086
Do I go in?

706
01:13:49.111 --> 01:13:52.078
I don't know.
It's never done that before.

707
01:14:10.495 --> 01:14:11.996
Khadgar.

708
01:14:12.021 --> 01:14:15.367
I know you,
from the library.

709
01:14:17.074 --> 01:14:18.838
You're Alodi?

710
01:14:22.234 --> 01:14:27.620
I used the last of my energies
to summon you here.

711
01:14:27.645 --> 01:14:31.727
- The Guardian has betrayed us.
- Medivh.

712
01:14:32.898 --> 01:14:36.803
- I saw the fel in his eyes.
- He is consumed by it.

713
01:14:36.828 --> 01:14:41.252
If he is not stopped,
this world will burn.

714
01:14:41.277 --> 01:14:43.806
I don't have the power
to defeat a Guardian.

715
01:14:44.785 --> 01:14:47.297
Guardian is but a name.

716
01:14:47.499 --> 01:14:52.302
The true Guardians of this world
are the people themselves.

717
01:14:52.327 --> 01:14:55.904
I know you see what
the Kirin Tor can not.

718
01:14:55.929 --> 01:14:57.927
It's why you left them.

719
01:14:57.952 --> 01:15:05.192
No one can stand against
the darkness... alone.

720
01:15:05.572 --> 01:15:08.316
I don't understand what
you want me to do.

721
01:15:11.697 --> 01:15:13.840
Yes, you do.

722
01:15:17.084 --> 01:15:19.507
Trust in your friends.

723
01:15:19.860 --> 01:15:23.099
Together, you can save this world.

724
01:15:23.124 --> 01:15:25.981
Always remember.

725
01:15:26.006 --> 01:15:28.591
From light comes darkness,

726
01:15:28.616 --> 01:15:33.403
and from darkness... light.

727
01:15:43.858 --> 01:15:45.371
Up, up.

728
01:15:52.026 --> 01:15:54.904
Thank you, Moroes.

729
01:15:55.475 --> 01:15:57.536
You'll recover, Guardian.

730
01:15:57.561 --> 01:15:59.230
You always do.

731
01:15:59.986 --> 01:16:04.267
No...
Thank you.

732
01:16:04.707 --> 01:16:06.937
For everything you've done.

733
01:16:23.049 --> 01:16:25.122
Sorry, old friend.

734
01:16:26.588 --> 01:16:31.592
It seems I have let
the orcs into this world.

735
01:16:31.752 --> 01:16:35.644
The fel has twisted me.
I...

736
01:16:35.676 --> 01:16:38.907
... don't even know
what else I may have done.

737
01:16:39.971 --> 01:16:43.673
I just don't remember.

738
01:16:48.211 --> 01:16:54.018
Everything I fought to protect,
I have... destroyed.

739
01:16:54.844 --> 01:16:57.289
I can't control the fel.

740
01:17:00.924 --> 01:17:02.857
No one can.

741
01:17:14.277 --> 01:17:16.937
Five legions to block Deadwind Pass.

742
01:17:16.962 --> 01:17:21.800
Another ten here, here, and here,
along Redridge Mountains.

743
01:17:21.825 --> 01:17:23.188
Supply lines here.

744
01:17:23.213 --> 01:17:26.653
While the Eastern Sea hems
them in both south and east.

745
01:17:27.565 --> 01:17:31.706
If we hold these positions,
we will be at our strongest.

746
01:17:32.304 --> 01:17:33.440
Containment?

747
01:17:33.465 --> 01:17:35.064
Until there is a better option, yes.

748
01:17:35.109 --> 01:17:37.763
And where there is
10 times as many.

749
01:17:37.788 --> 01:17:39.289
What then?

750
01:17:40.993 --> 01:17:42.304
If there were easy answers...

751
01:17:42.329 --> 01:17:45.616
Our priority must be
to stop the gate from opening.

752
01:17:45.955 --> 01:17:48.010
Fail there, and it's
just a matter of time

753
01:17:48.035 --> 01:17:49.659
before they beat us
with sheer numbers.

754
01:17:49.684 --> 01:17:51.564
What do you suggest?

755
01:17:52.335 --> 01:17:54.618
Send everything we got.

756
01:17:55.464 --> 01:17:58.780
Destroy the gate, free our people,
and end the immediate threat.

757
01:17:58.805 --> 01:18:01.538
- And the Orcs that remain?
- We'll take care of them later.

758
01:18:01.563 --> 01:18:04.066
After they've ravaged the entire kingdom?

759
01:18:04.281 --> 01:18:07.084
- My Lords.
- Medivh. You are up and well.

760
01:18:07.109 --> 01:18:12.125
I am.
I feel... restored.

761
01:18:12.150 --> 01:18:15.084
We need you.
We've been agonizing over our options.

762
01:18:15.109 --> 01:18:17.123
Some of us believe
there are no options.

763
01:18:17.148 --> 01:18:19.877
- We need fresh eyes.
- I have news.

764
01:18:19.902 --> 01:18:23.023
- I've met with Durotan.
- You met with Durotan.

765
01:18:23.048 --> 01:18:27.207
The rebellion against Gul'dan
is gaining strength.

766
01:18:27.232 --> 01:18:29.430
With their help we can
destroy this gate.

767
01:18:29.455 --> 01:18:32.260
- That doesn't change my plan.
- What plan?

768
01:18:32.285 --> 01:18:35.206
Anduin believes we should
attack with full force.

769
01:18:35.231 --> 01:18:37.750
I'm concerned it leaves the rest
of the kingdom defenseless.

770
01:18:37.775 --> 01:18:41.635
How many legions would you need
to hold the orcs in place?

771
01:18:41.660 --> 01:18:45.054
Five for Deadwind Pass.
Ten for the Redridge Mountains.

772
01:18:45.079 --> 01:18:46.214
Ten more to protect the city.

773
01:18:46.239 --> 01:18:48.741
We've already lost 18 legions.

774
01:18:48.766 --> 01:18:52.377
- That leaves one, two, three.
- Can it be done, Medivh?

775
01:18:52.402 --> 01:18:54.992
No, it can't be done.

776
01:18:56.041 --> 01:18:58.335
With three legion,
Frostwolves, and my power...

777
01:18:58.360 --> 01:18:59.968
With all due respect, Guardian,
your powers

778
01:18:59.993 --> 01:19:03.298
have proven unreliable
at best recently.

779
01:19:03.542 --> 01:19:05.527
- Llane. Have I ever let you down?
- Let him down?

780
01:19:05.552 --> 01:19:08.370
Where have you even been
for the last 6 years?

781
01:19:09.388 --> 01:19:11.147
Please, Anduin.
Medivh is the Guardian...

782
01:19:11.172 --> 01:19:13.425
Not the one you remember.

783
01:19:13.911 --> 01:19:16.261
He's lost it.
He's unstable.

784
01:19:16.286 --> 01:19:18.828
And he won't be there
when you really need him.

785
01:19:18.853 --> 01:19:20.931
Find your bearings, Anduin.

786
01:19:20.955 --> 01:19:23.073
I'd march into hell for you,

787
01:19:23.099 --> 01:19:25.713
if I thought there was a
slightest chance of victory.

788
01:19:25.738 --> 01:19:28.155
But there isn't,
this is suicide.

789
01:19:28.180 --> 01:19:30.185
Is this about Callan?

790
01:19:30.936 --> 01:19:32.558
It was a tragedy.

791
01:19:32.583 --> 01:19:35.408
If he hadn't been trying so hard
to win your approval,

792
01:19:35.433 --> 01:19:38.154
- he might still be with us.
- Medivh.

793
01:19:38.179 --> 01:19:40.299
Callan wasn't ready.
You knew it.

794
01:19:40.323 --> 01:19:43.261
- And you let him play soldier anyway.
- Anduin, stop!

795
01:19:43.286 --> 01:19:44.989
You killed him!

796
01:19:45.909 --> 01:19:48.200
Commander.
Please, sir. Please.

797
01:19:48.225 --> 01:19:51.679
Varis.
Take him to a cell to calm down.

798
01:19:52.765 --> 01:19:55.077
You are no use
to us like this.

799
01:20:06.866 --> 01:20:09.535
We'll protect the kingdom, my lord.

800
01:20:09.761 --> 01:20:11.505
You and I.

801
01:20:24.414 --> 01:20:25.987
Why are you here?

802
01:20:26.012 --> 01:20:27.656
The king.

803
01:20:28.537 --> 01:20:30.785
He goes to fight the Horde.

804
01:20:32.538 --> 01:20:36.081
With your Guardian's help,
Durotan will kill Gul'dan.

805
01:20:36.106 --> 01:20:37.274
Don't trust him.

806
01:20:37.299 --> 01:20:39.273
I've told you,
Orcs do not lie.

807
01:20:39.298 --> 01:20:41.068
Not Durotan.

808
01:20:44.276 --> 01:20:46.213
Don't trust Medivh.

809
01:20:50.756 --> 01:20:53.136
I will try to
protect your king.

810
01:20:53.557 --> 01:20:55.448
Don't go with them.

811
01:20:55.473 --> 01:20:56.838
Why?

812
01:20:59.478 --> 01:21:01.380
I don't want you
to get hurt.

813
01:21:15.294 --> 01:21:17.292
Come back alive.

814
01:21:39.772 --> 01:21:41.781
Hey, Frostwolf.

815
01:21:41.806 --> 01:21:43.312
Who goes...

816
01:21:44.878 --> 01:21:47.113
Now you are enemies
with all sides.

817
01:21:47.138 --> 01:21:49.268
I'll tell them it was you.

818
01:22:03.249 --> 01:22:05.044
What happened?

819
01:22:06.980 --> 01:22:09.286
I'm sorry, Durotan.

820
01:22:10.219 --> 01:22:13.307
I did not see how we could
side with the humans...

821
01:22:13.332 --> 01:22:15.736
against our own kind.

822
01:22:16.595 --> 01:22:18.509
I was wrong.

823
01:22:18.704 --> 01:22:21.999
Gul'dan's fel magic is destroying us.

824
01:22:30.543 --> 01:22:32.835
Where's Draka?
Safe?

825
01:22:32.860 --> 01:22:35.015
But, the rest...

826
01:22:36.931 --> 01:22:39.008
They won't follow him,

827
01:22:39.040 --> 01:22:41.525
if they could see
what he has become.

828
01:22:43.487 --> 01:22:45.665
And I will show them.

829
01:23:12.442 --> 01:23:16.665
There is no other man I would entrust
the safety of my family to, Varian.

830
01:23:16.962 --> 01:23:20.154
Keep them safe
while I'm gone.

831
01:23:33.128 --> 01:23:34.562
Ready?

832
01:23:35.290 --> 01:23:38.185
I would feel better if
Lothar were riding with us.

833
01:23:38.210 --> 01:23:40.077
We'll be fine.

834
01:23:40.102 --> 01:23:43.121
I'll return to Karazhan
and get ready for battle.

835
01:23:44.025 --> 01:23:45.963
Find me at the portal.

836
01:23:58.960 --> 01:24:00.789
Whoa. Whoa.
Whoa, whoa!

837
01:24:08.009 --> 01:24:09.413
Guard.

838
01:24:09.671 --> 01:24:13.754
I know you're just doing your job,
and a good one at that.

839
01:24:14.995 --> 01:24:17.201
But I've cool down now.

840
01:24:17.226 --> 01:24:20.370
So, if you just come
and open this gate.

841
01:24:20.395 --> 01:24:22.657
So I can protect the king.

842
01:24:25.020 --> 01:24:26.455
OPEN THE GATE !

843
01:24:26.480 --> 01:24:28.547
I am just following my...

844
01:24:35.557 --> 01:24:38.013
- Where the hell have you been?
- The Kirin Tor.

845
01:24:38.753 --> 01:24:41.850
It only works on the simple minded,
last about a minute.

846
01:24:42.416 --> 01:24:44.252
Your armor, commander.

847
01:24:45.018 --> 01:24:46.478
Sorry.

848
01:24:50.505 --> 01:24:52.587
They have a full day
ahead of us.

849
01:24:53.174 --> 01:24:55.745
- I just hope we're not too late.
- We can't go after them.

850
01:24:55.770 --> 01:24:57.099
Not if you want to save Azeroth.

851
01:24:57.124 --> 01:25:00.019
- My king needs me.
- AZEROTH needs you more!

852
01:25:00.308 --> 01:25:04.223
If you want to save your king,
we need to stop Medivh first.

853
01:25:14.129 --> 01:25:15.923
Where is Medivh?

854
01:25:16.699 --> 01:25:18.825
We got a demon to kill.

855
01:25:24.090 --> 01:25:26.497
Go.
Search over here.

856
01:25:44.708 --> 01:25:46.290
Remember.

857
01:25:46.315 --> 01:25:48.577
You are the son of
Durotan and Draka,

858
01:25:48.602 --> 01:25:51.234
an unbroken line of chieftains.

859
01:26:39.602 --> 01:26:43.908
I am Durotan,
son of Garad.

860
01:26:44.714 --> 01:26:47.339
Chieftain of the Frostwolf clan.

861
01:26:47.364 --> 01:26:51.526
And I am here
to kill Gul'dan.

862
01:26:52.367 --> 01:26:56.012
Ghost cannot invoke Mak'gora.
(Duel of honor)

863
01:26:56.037 --> 01:26:58.730
You are the chieftain
of no clan.

864
01:26:58.755 --> 01:27:01.764
Your people are food for worms.

865
01:27:02.386 --> 01:27:05.628
Some of us still live, warchief.

866
01:27:09.306 --> 01:27:11.768
Do I make
a quick end of them?

867
01:27:12.016 --> 01:27:15.637
I always thought you were
one for tradition, Blackhand.

868
01:27:17.820 --> 01:27:19.657
Durotan.

869
01:27:20.958 --> 01:27:25.397
Your clan was weak,
and you are a traitor.

870
01:27:26.254 --> 01:27:29.223
I accept your challenge,
if only to personally

871
01:27:29.248 --> 01:27:32.421
ripped the heart out
of your pathetic body.

872
01:27:32.446 --> 01:27:33.775
What of the portal?

873
01:27:33.800 --> 01:27:36.967
You must be ready when
the incantation begins

874
01:27:37.269 --> 01:27:39.640
This won't take long.

875
01:29:03.979 --> 01:29:06.128
Crush him, Gul'dan!

876
01:29:15.990 --> 01:29:18.678
It's the incantation
to the Orc home world.

877
01:29:21.006 --> 01:29:23.704
He's opening the portal,
we need to shut him up.

878
01:29:27.227 --> 01:29:29.258
The incantation.

879
01:29:29.607 --> 01:29:33.297
I have no time for this.
Blackhand!

880
01:29:35.059 --> 01:29:37.571
(... Orc tradition...)

881
01:29:38.824 --> 01:29:41.286
This is a Mak'gora.
(Duel of honor)

882
01:29:42.861 --> 01:29:45.550
You will respect our tradition.

883
01:29:45.885 --> 01:29:47.890
Keep fighting.

884
01:29:54.507 --> 01:29:56.640
Gul'dan cheats.

885
01:30:05.339 --> 01:30:07.009
- Cheating!
- Shame on you!

886
01:30:07.034 --> 01:30:09.121
You cheat, Gul'dan!

887
01:30:09.146 --> 01:30:10.996
This is not our way.

888
01:30:11.021 --> 01:30:13.105
Traitor!

889
01:30:28.434 --> 01:30:30.358
GUL'DAN !

890
01:30:32.446 --> 01:30:35.463
You have no honor.

891
01:31:20.280 --> 01:31:23.989
You will follow this... thing?

892
01:31:29.036 --> 01:31:30.502
Do you?

893
01:31:33.840 --> 01:31:36.371
You will follow this demon?

894
01:31:37.764 --> 01:31:39.635
I will not.

895
01:31:41.540 --> 01:31:44.654
I follow a true Orc.

896
01:31:45.901 --> 01:31:47.747
A chieftain.

897
01:31:53.526 --> 01:31:56.674
May your balls rot, demon.

898
01:32:01.451 --> 01:32:03.457
Anyone else?

899
01:32:07.038 --> 01:32:09.619
And you, warchief.

900
01:32:09.643 --> 01:32:11.115
You will take the fel,

901
01:32:11.140 --> 01:32:14.648
and you will become stronger
than any Orc has ever been.

902
01:32:14.674 --> 01:32:20.174
And when the fel has remade you,
you will crush the smallteeth.

903
01:32:22.750 --> 01:32:25.971
Now claim my new world.

904
01:32:33.622 --> 01:32:35.465
Legion!
Halt!

905
01:32:35.490 --> 01:32:37.291
Frostwolves.

906
01:32:39.373 --> 01:32:41.683
We are on our own now.

907
01:32:41.708 --> 01:32:43.556
With you then.

908
01:32:53.112 --> 01:32:55.037
Get to the prisoners.

909
01:32:55.179 --> 01:32:57.548
We will free our people!

910
01:32:58.365 --> 01:33:00.090
Charge!

911
01:33:08.959 --> 01:33:10.908
Attack!

912
01:33:12.902 --> 01:33:14.630
Ideas?

913
01:33:19.889 --> 01:33:24.333
Very impressive.
Now try shutting him up.

914
01:33:26.482 --> 01:33:28.335
Oh, that went well.

915
01:33:28.709 --> 01:33:31.071
Ohhhhh.

916
01:33:31.667 --> 01:33:34.639
- He's moving, do something.
- (What?)

917
01:33:34.664 --> 01:33:37.409
Fine, I'll handle this.

918
01:33:38.000 --> 01:33:40.064
You take care of Medivh.

919
01:33:47.160 --> 01:33:50.205
Hey, over here.
Clayface.

920
01:34:09.559 --> 01:34:11.422
Now, men!

921
01:34:11.949 --> 01:34:13.635
Fire!

922
01:35:01.191 --> 01:35:03.151
Come, my orcs.

923
01:35:03.176 --> 01:35:07.985
Let the fel unleash the
full power of the Horde.

924
01:35:15.440 --> 01:35:18.630
- For Gul'dan!
- For the Horde!

925
01:36:05.434 --> 01:36:08.292
Hey, kid!
Wake up!

926
01:36:10.559 --> 01:36:12.228
You alright?

927
01:36:14.542 --> 01:36:16.059
Quick thinking.

928
01:36:16.084 --> 01:36:18.449
- Slicing it's head off like that.
- Yeah.

929
01:36:18.474 --> 01:36:20.291
Just how I planned it.

930
01:36:21.724 --> 01:36:22.912
What now?

931
01:36:22.937 --> 01:36:25.923
The Guardian has to speak
the incantation himself.

932
01:36:25.948 --> 01:36:28.305
So uh...
As long as he is doing that...

933
01:36:28.334 --> 01:36:31.689
... we can get in close.
Distract him.

934
01:36:32.040 --> 01:36:33.654
Then what?

935
01:36:34.338 --> 01:36:36.418
Get Medivh in the font.

936
01:36:36.779 --> 01:36:38.584
Is that all?

937
01:36:50.880 --> 01:36:52.438
Medivh.

938
01:36:52.954 --> 01:36:56.310
If there is something of you
still in there, old friend,

939
01:36:57.809 --> 01:36:59.603
come back to us.

940
01:37:19.680 --> 01:37:21.317
Medivh.

941
01:37:32.449 --> 01:37:33.790
Come.

942
01:37:34.558 --> 01:37:36.103
Kill me.

943
01:37:37.630 --> 01:37:41.001
I have got nothing left
to live for now anyway.

944
01:37:44.438 --> 01:37:47.710
After all, life is just
fuel to you, isn't it?

945
01:37:48.629 --> 01:37:51.712
But Llane, he believed in you.

946
01:37:52.854 --> 01:37:54.704
Don't kill your king.

947
01:37:56.399 --> 01:37:58.365
Don't kill your friend.

948
01:38:06.075 --> 01:38:08.372
Whatever you plan to do, kid.

949
01:38:08.859 --> 01:38:10.441
Do it now.

950
01:38:16.047 --> 01:38:17.421
Now.

951
01:38:18.911 --> 01:38:20.878
Now!
Now!

952
01:38:20.903 --> 01:38:22.795
Now, kid!

953
01:38:30.297 --> 01:38:32.508
The portal.
It's closing!

954
01:38:32.533 --> 01:38:34.011
No.

955
01:39:06.049 --> 01:39:08.283
You're stronger than he is.

956
01:39:25.343 --> 01:39:28.156
From light comes darkness...

957
01:39:29.054 --> 01:39:32.839
and from darkness... light.

958
01:39:50.012 --> 01:39:51.982
Show me your eyes.

959
01:40:00.555 --> 01:40:02.235
I have to go.

960
01:40:08.686 --> 01:40:10.510
I'm proud of you.

961
01:40:37.467 --> 01:40:39.186
Stormwind.

962
01:40:40.183 --> 01:40:43.762
My lord.
Through the portal, Stormwind!

963
01:40:43.787 --> 01:40:45.667
Thank you, Guardian.

964
01:40:45.763 --> 01:40:46.894
Varis!

965
01:40:46.919 --> 01:40:49.559
Legion, forward!

966
01:40:50.272 --> 01:40:51.937
Attack!

967
01:40:52.433 --> 01:40:54.845
Garona, ride with me.

968
01:41:19.866 --> 01:41:22.100
Varis, set the men
in a perimeter.

969
01:41:22.125 --> 01:41:25.680
Garona, Karos, take what men
we can spare and free the prisoners.

970
01:41:25.704 --> 01:41:27.614
And send them through to Stormwind.

971
01:41:27.639 --> 01:41:29.435
Form a line,
shield to shield!

972
01:41:29.460 --> 01:41:31.988
We will hold
as long as we can.

973
01:41:33.269 --> 01:41:35.079
Get to the portal.

974
01:41:36.238 --> 01:41:38.656
- Go.
- Bless you.

975
01:41:38.856 --> 01:41:40.357
Thank you.

976
01:41:56.323 --> 01:41:58.267
I need more powder.

977
01:41:59.899 --> 01:42:03.481
Get over there!
Help me push!

978
01:42:04.492 --> 01:42:08.927
Come on, boys!
Put your scorn into it!

979
01:42:16.379 --> 01:42:20.683
Go around!
We'll attack them behind the portal!

980
01:42:30.336 --> 01:42:32.303
Take care of him.

981
01:42:38.239 --> 01:42:39.748
We should leave.

982
01:42:39.773 --> 01:42:42.770
We save as many of
our people as we can.

983
01:42:46.827 --> 01:42:51.637
It's the loneliness
that makes us weak.

984
01:42:52.438 --> 01:42:54.065
Khadgar.

985
01:42:56.724 --> 01:42:58.427
I'm sorry.

986
01:43:00.023 --> 01:43:02.476
I wanted to save us all.

987
01:43:05.528 --> 01:43:07.529
I always did.

988
01:43:18.444 --> 01:43:19.693
Move!

989
01:43:26.838 --> 01:43:28.840
We've lost the Guardian.

990
01:43:36.949 --> 01:43:40.780
Protect the flank!
Protect the flank!

991
01:44:11.917 --> 01:44:15.285
Blackhand comes to claim
the honor of killing you.

992
01:44:20.432 --> 01:44:22.013
Garona.

993
01:44:23.335 --> 01:44:26.007
No good will come
from us both died.

994
01:44:26.815 --> 01:44:30.488
Look around you,
we are surrounded.

995
01:44:32.036 --> 01:44:35.631
Your killing me is the only
hope we have for peace.

996
01:44:36.248 --> 01:44:40.432
You told Lady Taria that killing her
would bring you honor.

997
01:44:40.457 --> 01:44:43.404
Well. Killing me
would make you a hero.

998
01:44:46.746 --> 01:44:48.384
Survive.

999
01:44:49.121 --> 01:44:52.470
Bring peace between
orcs and humans.

1000
01:44:54.859 --> 01:44:56.754
You must.

1001
01:45:14.902 --> 01:45:16.713
You must.

1002
01:45:42.593 --> 01:45:44.511
No.
No!

1003
01:46:02.017 --> 01:46:05.130
She has killed their chieftain,
Gul'dan.

1004
01:46:05.728 --> 01:46:08.672
The Horde embraces you.

1005
01:46:10.606 --> 01:46:12.299
Orc.

1006
01:47:49.716 --> 01:47:52.002
Mak'gora.
(Duel of honor)

1007
01:49:05.851 --> 01:49:07.736
For my son.

1008
01:49:15.800 --> 01:49:17.278
Kill him.

1009
01:49:22.399 --> 01:49:24.388
Kill him!

1010
01:49:28.325 --> 01:49:32.111
Gul'dan, the Mak'gora is sacred.

1011
01:49:32.461 --> 01:49:35.490
The human won, fairly.

1012
01:49:36.258 --> 01:49:38.430
Let your warriors honor their tradition.

1013
01:49:38.455 --> 01:49:41.426
I will not be disobeyed.

1014
01:49:41.978 --> 01:49:44.662
What are you waiting for?

1015
01:49:49.974 --> 01:49:52.121
Do as I say!

1016
01:49:53.728 --> 01:49:55.520
Traitors!

1017
01:49:58.846 --> 01:50:02.040
Get out of my way,
I'll do it myself.

1018
01:50:02.065 --> 01:50:03.317
Who will obey you?

1019
01:50:03.342 --> 01:50:05.640
If you go to war
with your own kind.

1020
01:50:06.063 --> 01:50:09.479
If you do this,
you will lose the Horde.

1021
01:50:09.719 --> 01:50:11.977
And this war is only beginning.

1022
01:50:52.038 --> 01:50:54.018
For your son.

1023
01:50:57.920 --> 01:51:00.833
So your spirit can teach him.

1024
01:51:31.969 --> 01:51:33.723
Garona's dagger.

1025
01:51:34.827 --> 01:51:37.156
I pulled that from Llane's neck.

1026
01:51:37.181 --> 01:51:39.453
Well.
There has to be an explanation.

1027
01:51:39.478 --> 01:51:43.235
Yes.
She made her choice.

1028
01:51:44.198 --> 01:51:45.953
I don't believe that.

1029
01:51:48.734 --> 01:51:52.229
Maybe you and I didn't know her
as well as we thought we did.

1030
01:51:55.843 --> 01:52:00.389
There is no greater blessing
a city can have

1031
01:52:00.414 --> 01:52:07.192
than a king who would
sacrifice himself for his people.

1032
01:52:09.312 --> 01:52:12.635
But such a sacrifice must be earned.

1033
01:52:12.660 --> 01:52:14.762
We must deserve it.

1034
01:52:15.076 --> 01:52:19.969
If we only show our unity
to mourn a good man's death.

1035
01:52:20.014 --> 01:52:22.610
Was King Llane wrong
to believe in you?

1036
01:52:22.635 --> 01:52:25.314
- No!
- No!

1037
01:52:25.368 --> 01:52:27.917
We will avenge you, my lady!

1038
01:52:28.586 --> 01:52:31.761
Lead us against the orcs, Lothar!

1039
01:52:32.710 --> 01:52:37.274
- Lothar!
- Lothar!

1040
01:52:37.299 --> 01:52:40.999
- Lothar!
- Lothar!

1041
01:52:41.024 --> 01:52:44.883
- Lothar!
- Lothar!

1042
01:52:48.907 --> 01:52:52.888
For Azeroth!
For Azeroth and the Alliance!

1043
01:52:52.913 --> 01:52:55.419
- For Azeroth!
- For Azeroth!

1044
01:52:55.444 --> 01:52:58.162
- For the Alliance!
- For the Alliance!

1045
01:53:04.268 --> 01:53:07.749
WARCRAFT

1046
01:53:21.472 --> 01:53:24.621
You will travel far, my little Go'el.

1047
01:53:29.754 --> 01:53:33.888
My world maybe lost,
but this is your world now.

1048
01:53:34.613 --> 01:53:36.806
Take what you need from it.

1049
01:53:36.831 --> 01:53:41.218
Make a home for the orcs
and let no one stand in your way.

1050
01:53:43.728 --> 01:53:46.709
My lord.
You should see this.

1051
01:53:47.258 --> 01:53:50.768
You are the son of
Durotan and Draka,

1052
01:53:50.793 --> 01:53:53.281
an unbroken line of chieftains.

1053
01:53:53.306 --> 01:53:55.366
And our people need
a leader now...

1054
01:53:55.391 --> 01:53:57.232
... more than ever.

1055
01:54:00.769 --> 01:54:05.887
Subtitle created by - <font color="#ffff00">Aorion</font> -
